ToothFairy2 Challenge. By carefully modifying key parameters such as patch size, network topology, and data augmentation strategies, we significantly improved the model’s performance on this challenging dataset. Our approach effectively addresses the unique challenges posed by dental CBCT images, including the need for precise localization and class distinction, which are critical for accurate dental diagnostics and treatment planning.
Our experimental results demonstrate that our tailored nnU-Net configuration, combined with strategic postprocessing techniques, can achieve high levels of accuracy as evidenced by the Dice coefficient and HD95 metrics across both the F-cases and the entire dataset.
Although some advanced techniques like pretraining with MultiTalent and tooth instance segmentation did not improve results, our final model configuration achieved the first place on the leaderboard, highlighting its robustness and effectiveness.
